# CWYD-14, CWYD-20 — security headers and the API docs switch. Run against `docker compose up --build --wait`
# (VS Code / Cursor REST Client, or JetBrains HTTP Client). Check the response headers, not the body.

# From inside the dev container the published ports live on the host daemon
# (docker-outside-of-docker): set @host = host.docker.internal there.
@host = localhost
@api = http://{{host}}:8000
@web = http://{{host}}:8080

### SPA: 200 with X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin,
# X-Frame-Options: DENY, Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(),
# usb=() and Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; ... frame-ancestors 'none'.
# Server: nginx, without a version (CWYD-20); on every response below too.
HEAD {{web}}/

### Assets location: missing file, still 404 with the four headers and the location's own
# Cache-Control (an existing /assets/index-*.js, from the <script> tag of GET {{web}}/, gives 200)
HEAD {{web}}/assets/missing.js

### API through the proxy: 200 with nosniff, Referrer-Policy and X-Frame-Options, no CSP
GET {{web}}/api/health

# Upload rejected by nginx itself (body over 11 MB): 413 {"code":"file_too_large",...} with the
# four headers. Not a REST-client request (needs a large file):
#   head -c 12000000 /dev/zero > /tmp/big.txt && curl -si -F file=@/tmp/big.txt {{web}}/api/documents

### API docs, default API_DOCS_ENABLED=true: 200 for /docs, /redoc and /openapi.json
GET {{api}}/docs

###
GET {{api}}/openapi.json

### With API_DOCS_ENABLED=false in .env (then `docker compose up -d backend`):
# 404 {"detail":"Not Found"} for /docs, /redoc and /openapi.json; /health stays 200
GET {{api}}/redoc

### Swagger UI through the web server (CWYD-20): 200, the page loads url: '/api/openapi.json'
GET {{web}}/api/docs

### Spec through the web server: "servers": [{"url": "/api"}], so "Try it out" calls {{web}}/api/...
GET {{web}}/api/openapi.json

### "Try it out" on GET /health from {{web}}/api/docs: 200 {"status":"ok"}
GET {{web}}/api/health

### Swagger UI directly: 200, the page loads url: '/openapi.json' (no proxy header, no servers)
GET {{api}}/docs

### A prefix the API does not expect is ignored: the page still loads url: '/openapi.json'
GET {{api}}/docs
X-Forwarded-Prefix: /evil

### A path that already has the prefix is not routed through the web server: 404, so the
# rate-limited exact locations (DOM-27) cannot be skipped with /api/api/chat
POST {{web}}/api/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "q"}
